  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user whose list filter is Favoris, Suivis or Lus, I want a sub-forum to open with the two requests it needs, so that every sub-forum I open does not send a third one that is cancelled at once. Audit #1388, finding B2 (by reading; no app test run in the cloud).\n\n### What happens (read at `dev-swift` `1685bcc`)\n1. First load of a `.subforum` source: `subforumTarget` is nil, so the \"Tous\" page is fetched (`TopicListModel.swift:343-346`). GET 1, needed: only that page names the `subcat` (GAP-023).\n2. The load applies; `subforumTarget` is set (`:367`), so `offersFilter` turns true and `wantedFilter` becomes the stored filter. `load` then asks again itself: `if wantedFilter != loadedFilter { await load(page: 1) }` (`:377`). GET 2, needed.\n3. The same state change moves the id of `.task(id: model.wantedFilter)` (`TopicListView.swift:129`): SwiftUI starts `onAppear` again, which finds `wantedFilter != loadedFilter` (GET 2 is still in flight) and calls `load(page: 1)` too (`:285-287`). GET 3 supersedes GET 2, which is cancelled (`ContentLoader.swift:26-27`).\n\nCount: 3 requests, 1 cancelled in flight, for every sub-forum opened with a non-« Tous » filter. A cancelled request on the account session is also what #1191 / #1230 had to handle.\n\n### Proposed fix\nOne owner for \"the wanted filter changed\": either `load`'s own tail or the view task, not both. For example `onAppear` skips the filter branch while a load for the wanted filter is in flight (remember the filter of the load in flight), or the view task is keyed on something the first load does not change.\n\n### Test\nApp test with a counting `ForumDataSource`: open a sub-forum with the stored filter `.favorites`, signed in → exactly 2 `topicList` calls, none cancelled.\n\nRefs #1388.",
